      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.01,
          "end": 3.19,
          "en": "So before we start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.19,
          "end": 5.48,
          "en": "with sending HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.48,
          "end": 8.97,
          "en": "let's decide when we want to send requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.97,
          "end": 11.7,
          "en": "And there are a couple of places in the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 14.15,
          "en": "where we probably wanna do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.15,
          "end": 16.12,
          "en": "For example, in Manage Expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.12,
          "end": 20.96,
          "en": "when we save a new expense or update an existing expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.96,
          "end": 24.5,
          "en": "then we don't just wanna store it in our context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.5,
          "end": 28.58,
          "en": "we still might wanna do that so that we store a local copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.58,
          "end": 30.06,
          "en": "in memory as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 33.71,
          "en": "But we also want to send the expense to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.71,
          "end": 37.91,
          "en": "We wanna fetch expenses when we view our expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.91,
          "end": 41.52,
          "en": "for example, on the recent expenses JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.52,
          "end": 44.64,
          "en": "When we delete an expense in Manage Expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.64,
          "end": 46.97,
          "en": "we also wanna send a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.97,
          "end": 49.253,
          "en": "So that's where we wanna do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.09,
          "end": 53.44,
          "en": "Now, how do we send such requests though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.44,
          "end": 57.07,
          "en": "Well, in React Native, you can use the Fetch API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.07,
          "end": 59.46,
          "en": "that's also available in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 60.622,
          "en": "You can use this fetch function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.622,
          "end": 63.44,
          "en": "which you might know from the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.44,
          "end": 67.68,
          "en": "But React Native also supports XML, HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 70.28,
          "en": "and that means that you can also use libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.28,
          "end": 73.393,
          "en": "that build upon XML, HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.3,
          "end": 79.22,
          "en": "And a very popular library that does that is Axios.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.22,
          "end": 81.99,
          "en": "Axios is a promise-based HTTP client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.99,
          "end": 86.86,
          "en": "which you can use in the browser and also in React Native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.86,
          "end": 88.69,
          "en": "You might notice package already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.69,
          "end": 90.49,
          "en": "I like it a lot because it makes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.49,
          "end": 93.59,
          "en": "sending HTTP requests really easy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.59,
          "end": 96.45,
          "en": "and you could use the Fetch API as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 99.97,
          "en": "but here I will use Axios also to show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.97,
          "end": 102.348,
          "en": "how you can use that third-party API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.348,
          "end": 105.18,
          "en": "for sending such requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 107.83,
          "en": "We need to install Axios as a first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.83,
          "end": 110.75,
          "en": "And therefore, here in a new terminal window,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.75,
          "end": 114.053,
          "en": "I will run NPM install Axios in this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.1,
          "end": 118.47,
          "en": "And once it is installed, we can start using it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.47,
          "end": 121.44,
          "en": "for sending HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.44,
          "end": 123.63,
          "en": "And that is the offer, of what we will do next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
